    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Everything is green. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) passes, including the new `bulkSignupWarning` assertion \u2014 which confirms the field is generated into `OwnerDto`, mapped, and serialized as `false` for a fresh create.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `bulkSignupWarning` as a value assigned at registration and stored on the owner (mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` pattern), so both the POST create response and the GET read-back return the same, stable value.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the openapi-generator emits the DTO field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` `Boolean` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name (no explicit `@Mapping` needed).\n\n3. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's adjusted business day and sets the flag to `count > 80`. It reuses the exact accumulation path as `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` (the daily-limit rule rejects at `>= 100`; the warning fires above 80, so 81\u201399 are allowed-with-warning).\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `assignNamesakeCount` and before `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the count reflects owners already persisted and excludes the new one.\n\n5. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\nThe value is a snapshot at creation (\"more than 80 owners had *already been created* today\") and is never updated on PUT, consistent with the spec's per-registration derived fields.",
